```

This would replace any occurrences of "RESTAURANT" with just "Restaurant". You can modify this regex pattern to suit your specific needs.

Alternatively, you could use a more complex regex pattern to categorize the Facility Type into specific types:

```sql
SELECT 
  CASE 
    WHEN REGEXP_MATCH(Facility_Type, 'MOBILE FOOD DISPENSER') THEN 'Mobile Food Dispenser'
    WHEN REGEXP_MATCH(Facility_Type, 'RESTAURANT') THEN 'Restaurant'
    WHEN REGEXP_MATCH(Facility_Type, 'SCHOOL') THEN 'School'
    ELSE Facility_Type
  END AS Facility_Type,
  ...
FROM table_name;
```

This would categorize the Facility Type into specific types based on the regex patterns.

